  intel published that they will create  another 10 000 jobs indirect  to their investment activities so the  benefit coming out of those projects is  much higher than the amount paid for  starting such an activity and  you have to also consider  subsidies are part of investing  internationally so um the amount that is  paid in in europe and in germany this  time um is  not that high as it would be in for  example korea taiwan china or united  states so i think it's that is part of  attracting that is part of developing um  sustainable future technologies in  regions and i think that's part of the  commitment of the government to support  those developments just briefly if you  can you know a key strategy for the new  german government also for the eu is is  making us less dependent on technology  from the us or asia what needs to be  done to achieve that  i think um the the framework that i just  mentioned the  incentive scheme the clear  focus on certain industry sectors is  very important and the european  commission is focusing on certain  aspects the german government is  focusing on certain industry topics um  so a clear focus is helpful um the  german government decided on developing  a sustainable energy supply for example  so the clear focus is relevant i think  we're gonna have to leave it there sorry  we're out of time thank you so much for  joining us

